Columbus, April 15.—Adjutant General Weybrecht today received orders from Washington for the second detail of Ohio National Guard officers to report at San Antonio by April 25 to assist for fourteen days in the maneuvers by the army.

Those who probably will go are:
Major A. W. Davis, Fifth Infantry, Norwalk; Major G. W. Cunningham, Sixth Infantry, Fostoria; Captains L. L. Oyler, Fourth Infantry, Columbus; G. G. Sayre, Eighth Infantry, Gallon; L. B. Clancy, First Infantry, Batavia; Karl L. Best, Third Infantry, Dayton;

